sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-conus-second-assessor-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Model fidelity to source: 62/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "I verified by hand that the Boolean form l XOR (c OR r) and the GF(2) ANF reproduce the Rule 30 truth table (00011110), that run_eca uses the standard Wolfram neighbourhood indexing so Rule 90 is also correct, that Jen's inverse a_{t,i-1} = a_{t+1,i} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1}) follows algebraically and is applied with the right time offsets, that the diagonal recursion d_k(t+1) = d_{k-2}(t) XOR (d_{k-1}(t) OR d_k(t)) is an exact change of variables, and that the three Boolean partial derivatives are right; the CA half is exemplary. The Meinhardt-Klingler half is a loose analogue, not the published equations: autocatalysis is divided by a relaxation variable b with db/dt = mu_b (a - b), which is neither the 1987 activator-depleted-substrate system nor the hormone that modulates activator decay in the Oliva model, parameter names and values are unsourced, and a stochastic rule injecting +0.90 activator at random high-substrate sites plus hard clipping of a, s, b is load-bearing (with the injection removed the pattern extinguishes to 0.9 percent pigment in steps 148-221 and a saturates at the 5.0 clip); deduction 20. The Raup mesh uses W^(theta/2pi) and r_c = a(1+D)/(1-D) correctly but replaces Raup's generating curve with an ad hoc envelope carrying six unsourced constants, so that T has no effect on the silhouette for T in [0, 0.36]; deduction 10. Remaining 8 points lost for over-naming a sufficiency check as an iff theorem, a 0.36 vs 0.40 D2 mismatch in the bioelectric panel, and cross-model panels that are toy re-implementations. Evidence: 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L140–L182: Rule 30 Boolean/ANF steps, generic ECA evolution and Jen left inverse; all verified against the truth table and algebra <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L140-L182>; 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L296–L318: Diagonal recursion d_k(t+1)=d_{k-2}^(d_{k-1}|d_k) is an exact coordinate change; 0 errors confirmed on re-run <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L296-L318>; 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L645–L660: PDE: production divided by relaxation variable b, random +0.90 activator injection with p=0.18 per substep, and clipping; not the published M&K equations and the injection is load-bearing <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L645-L660>; 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L691–L704: Ad hoc biconical envelope (0.468, 1.28, 0.78, 1.05, 1.55, 0.42) replaces Raup's generating curve; Z extent set by S*axial_ext so T is swamped <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L691-L704>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-model-fidelity> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.62"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-model-fidelity> rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation (1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py, docs/media/conus_textile_rule30.gif, docs/media/conus_rule30_kymograph_defect_fronts.png, conus_textile_rule30_metrics.csv, conus_rule30_defect_fronts.csv) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Model fidelity to source' for Conus textile Linnaeus, 1758 (textile cone snail)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Cursor agent, blinded second assessor)" .
}

